  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b53d3a7811bb8498d9ae0485fd422ad9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Day2_Scam_Room
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: DontCallMe::DontCallMe.Data.RoomContent
  newspaper:
    masthead: SEOUL DAILY
    issue: No. 12,409
    dateLine: WEDNESDAY, OCTOBER 7, 2026
    price: 1,000 won
    headline: '"Protection team" scam calls hit Mangwon'
    subhead: Callers posing as Nuri Bank staff asked residents to move their savings
      to a stranger's account.
    photo: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 4c63c0d2cf38942db834f06de02c655f, type: 3}
    caption: 'Before any transfer, the bank shows who really gets the money. Photo:
      Seoul Daily'
    body:
    - A caller calling himself "Manager Jeon" of Nuri Bank's "account protection
      team" phoned residents of Mangwon-dong yesterday afternoon. He warned them
      that their accounts had been accessed from Busan and asked them to move their
      savings to a "protected account" before a 5 p.m. "security reset".
    - Several residents hung up. Police say the "protected account", Nuri Bank 110-900-551207,
      belongs to a 30-year-old woman paid to lend her account to the ring, and ask
      anyone called by 070-8844-2019 to report it to 112 or the fraud hotline 1332.
    - '"There is no such thing as a protected account," said Song Eunji of Nuri Bank''s
      customer centre. "Look up whose account it is before you send anything. If
      it''s a person''s name, stop and hang up."'
    warningTitle: 'RENT DAY: CHECK THE NEW ACCOUNT'
    warningText: 'Tenants across Mapo report calls about a "new rent account" around
      rent day. Not every bad account has reports yet, so check who is behind it:
      is the account in the name of your landlord or someone your lease names? Is
      the caller''s number in your lease?'
    print: {fileID: 0}
    local:
    - title: Water tank cleaning tomorrow
      text: Villas on Poeun-ro will be without water on Thursday, 10:00-12:00.
    - title: Mangwon market by night
      text: The market stays open until 23:00 this Saturday, with street food and
        live music.
    - title: Midterms
      text: Hanbit University's library opens around the clock from Friday.
    ads:
    - title: "\uCE58\uD0A8 CHICKEN 24H"
      text: Crispy & soy garlic. Free delivery over 20,000 won. 02-555-0147
    - title: CHECKFIRST.KR
      text: Who owns that number? Whose account is it? Look it up before you send.
    - title: HANBIT ACADEMY
      text: TOEIC weekend class, 30% off for students. 02-555-0166
  drawer:
  - title: "Lease contract \xB7 Unit 302"
    kind: 0
    issuer: Mangwon Heights
    fields:
    - label: Landlord
      value: Choi Youngsik
      isFact: 0
      factKind: 6
    - label: Landlord's phone
      value: 010-5512-3380
      isFact: 1
      factKind: 0
    - label: Rent
      value: 450,000 won a month, due on the 7th
      isFact: 0
      factKind: 6
    - label: Rent account
      value: 110-771-209944
      isFact: 1
      factKind: 1
    - label: Account holder
      value: Choi Youngsik (Nuri Bank)
      isFact: 0
      factKind: 6
    - label: If absent, contact
      value: Choi Hyunwoo (son)
      isFact: 0
      factKind: 6
    - label: Son's phone
      value: 010-2280-6614
      isFact: 1
      factKind: 0
    body: 'Special terms

      1. The rent account changes only with a written notice
      from the landlord.

      2. The tenant allows the annual gas safety inspection.

      3.
      No smoking inside the unit.'
    stamp: 
    image: {fileID: 0}
